How to FIND the target rotation.

WHAT IS targetRotation?
It is simply:
“The rotation you WANT your object to reach.”
Your object will rotate from current rotation → to targetRotation. So the question becomes:

WAY 2 — Using LookRotation (toward a direction)
Vector3 dir = target.position - transform.position;
Quaternion targetRotation = Quaternion.LookRotation(dir);

------------------------------------------------------
Using current rotation + change
Quaternion targetRotation = transform.rotation * Quaternion.Euler(0, 90, 0);
targetRotation = Quaternion.LookRotation(target.position - transform.position);

A flowchart: How to choose targetRotation
Do you want to rotate TO a specific angle?

                ┌──→ Need to face TARGET? ───→ LookRotation(dir)
                │
                ├──→ Need to face DIRECTION? → LookRotation(direction)
                │
START → What →  ├──→ Rotate TO ANGLE? ───────→ Quaternion.Euler(x,y,z)
rotation?       │
                ├──→ Rotate BY ANGLE? ───────→ current * Quaternion.Euler()
                │
                ├──→ Smooth rotation? ───────→ Lerp / Slerp / RotateTowards
                │
                ├──→ Physics rotation? ─────→ Rigidbody.MoveRotation()
                │
                └──→ Limit rotation? ────────→ Clamp + Quaternion.Euler()
